Alembic migrations, driven by __PACKAGE__.migrations.

  alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add widgets"   # write a migration
  alembic upgrade head                               # apply it
  alembic downgrade -1                               # undo the last one
  alembic upgrade head --sql                         # print the SQL instead

The database url comes from the environment (DB_HOST, DB_USER, DB_PASSWORD,
DB_NAME), not from alembic.ini -- the same variables the application reads.

Always read a generated migration before committing it. Autogenerate does not
detect renames (it emits a drop plus an add, which loses the data), and cannot
know what to backfill for a new NOT NULL column.
